tside spending on both sides", "Raters nearly unanimous: Tossup, with one Tilt R"], "rationale": "Recent polls put Turek up by roughly a point on average, but markets and one rater lean toward Hinson, and Iowa's Republican baseline cuts against a Democrat. The evidence nets out to an even race, so the forecast sits at a dead-even margin with wide uncertainty.", "watch": "A late debate-driven shift or movement in the governor's race turnout could tip either way.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Joni Ernst (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Iowa's open Senate seat is one of the closest races of 2026. Joni Ernst's retirement left Republicans with Ashley Hinson, a strong fundraiser with $6.7 million on hand, against Democrat Josh Turek, who has benefited from nearly $10 million in outside support. Recent polls show Turek narrowly ahead, with several surveys putting him up one to four points, though some Republican-leaning pollsters show Hinson in front.\n\nExpert raters call the race a Tossup almost unanimously, while prediction markets give Hinson a modest edge. Iowa's six-point Republican lean offsets the favorable polling environment Democrats appear to be enjoying, leaving the race genuinely even heading into the final weeks.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.6012, "margin": 1.25}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.5782, "margin": 0.8}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.5857, "margin": 0.8}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.5846, "margin": 0.8}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.4983, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.503, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.579, "margin": 0.8}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.5896, "margin": 0.8}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.5557, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.499, "margin": -0.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.5985, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.607, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.6056, "margin